Error [jet.TypestateWrongState]: `ship` needs `Order` in state `Confirmed`, but `order` may be in state `Draft`
  --> tests/ui/typestate/paths_meeting_in_different_states_reject_a_state_call.jet:19:11
    |
 19 |     order.ship()
    |           ^^^^
 Why: Typestate: paths that leave `order` in `Confirmed` and `Draft` meet before this, so `ship` may run in `Draft`, the out-of-order-events bug it prevents
 Fix: Bring every path to `Confirmed` before they meet, or call `ship` inside the path that reaches `Confirmed`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0150
